## 1. EXECUTIVE PRODUCT DIRECTION

This direction comes from the latest Ravi and Dheeraj product review.

Important decisions:

1. Focus on building an AI Native EHR first. Full Hospital Management System functionality is not the current priority.
2. Continue using this existing Google AI Studio application as the primary prototype.
3. Preserve the clean existing EigenH interface.
4. Focus on one successful patient journey before expanding into unrelated modules.
5. Make the clinician experience dramatically simpler.
6. Reduce manual data entry, clicks, screen switching and duplicated work.
7. Build two prominent clinician experiences:
   - Pre-Consultation Summary
   - Post-Consultation Summary
8. Introduce appropriately governed AI assistance throughout the patient journey.
9. Use accurate clinical terminology.
10. Support roles and clearly defined handoffs.
11. Make the complete experience demonstrable automatically without the presenter manually navigating and typing through every screen.
12. Preserve the original underlying clinical records, detailed chart views, and workflows even when creating simpler interfaces.

Our first priority scenario is the SCHEDULED PATIENT JOURNEY.

Walk-in and emergency journeys are not the first-priority demo.

The final product direction is:

"EHR intelligence should prepare information, reduce work, and coordinate the next action while qualified healthcare professionals retain clinical control."

## 2. MOST IMPORTANT NEW FEATURE: EIGENH AI DEMO DIRECTOR

Create a prominent new application feature called:

**EigenH AI Demo Director**

This must behave like an interactive video player controlling the ACTUAL EHR interface.

It is NOT a pre-recorded video.

It is NOT a slide deck.

It is NOT an animated mockup disconnected from the application.

It must be a reproducible, scenario-driven demonstration of the working synthetic application.

### Desired experience

A presenter opens Demo Scenarios, selects "Scheduled Patient Journey", and clicks Play.

The application automatically:

1. Shows the responsible role.
2. Opens the correct EHR screen.
3. Highlights the relevant interface control.
4. Explains the upcoming action.
5. Performs the actual permitted synthetic workflow operation.
6. Populates relevant fields.
7. Shows the resulting state change.
8. Opens the next connected screen.
9. Shows the receiving role and handoff.
10. Continues until the journey is complete.

The presenter should not have to manually type patient details, switch roles, navigate ten tabs, or repeat the same explanations during each demo.

### Demo Director controls

Implement:

